          "guid": "mtfusxwiitkcdsm5",
          "message": {
            "text": "Release readiness now follows the end-to-end product path, while the 498-difference standalone-Skia/Chromium comparison remains available as diagnostic evidence. This preserves exact logical and visual defect investigation without making equality between two intentionally different collector boundaries a prerequisite for macOS, Linux, or Windows functionality.",
            "markdown": "Release readiness now follows the end-to-end product path, while the 498-difference standalone-Skia/Chromium comparison remains available as diagnostic evidence. This preserves exact logical and visual defect investigation without making equality between two intentionally different collector boundaries a prerequisite for macOS, Linux, or Windows functionality."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/168-sfns-mask-baseline-oracle.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 39,
                  "endLine": 55,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "## Release requirement (DM-2604)\n\nThe exact standalone-Skia versus instrumented-Chromium terminal-mask\nadjudication is retained as an optional macOS diagnostic, not a release gate or\na prerequisite for claiming that Domotion functions on macOS, Linux, and\nWindows. The two collectors intentionally cross different ownership boundaries;\ntheir 498 literal differences remain useful leads when a visual regression\npoints at SFNS, but zero cross-collector byte equality is no longer a product\nrequirement.\n\nThree-platform functional tests and visual demo/Unicode sweeps remain the\nrelease-facing contract. A failing or suspicious visual fixture must be traced\nthrough the existing logical, placement, metric, outline, and raster evidence\nas needed; this change does not permit hiding an observed product defect or\nwidening a visual threshold. The optional workflow and retained artifacts stay\navailable for targeted investigation.\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
